        <headline>High Wind Warning issued September 26 at 1:47PM EDT until September 27 at 12:00PM EDT by NWS Upton NY</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Northeast winds 25 to 35 mph with gusts up to 65 mph.

* WHERE...In Connecticut, Northern New London, Southern Middlesex,
and Southern New London Counties. In New York, Northeast Suffolk,
Northern Nassau, Northwest Suffolk, Southeast Suffolk, Southern
Nassau, and Southwest Suffolk Counties.

* WHEN...Until noon EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.
Widespread power outages are expected. Travel will be difficult,
especially for high profile vehicles.
</description>
        <instruction>People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around
or damaged by the wind.

Remain in the lower levels of your home during the windstorm, and
avoid windows. Watch for falling debris and tree limbs. Use caution
if you must drive.</instruction>
